{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TensorPictureGenerator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TensorPictureGenerator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_Y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_Y","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L140-L143","doc":"`Y` is traceless against the pivotal weight at `q = 1` — the two-site form of\n`Tr(Y·P) = 0`, which the probes use for every permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.swap4_mul_Y_anticomm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.swap4_mul_Y_anticomm","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L130-L138","doc":"The first-order term minus the identity is `Y = diag(0, −1, 1, 0)`, and `Y`\nanticommutes with the swap — the concrete instance of\n`LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.hecke_first_order_anticommutes`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.diagPart_one_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.diagPart_one_add","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L118-L128","doc":"`q − 1 = ε` and `q − q⁻¹ = 2ε − ε² + ε³/(1+ε)`: the diagonal part at\n`q = 1 + ε` is `ε·diag(1, 0, 2, 1) + ε²·diag(0, 0, −1, 0) + ε³·diag(0, 0, 1/(1+ε), 0)`.\nSo `X = 1 + Y` with `Y = diag(0, −1, 1, 0)` and `W = diag(0, 0, −1, 0)`, exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_pivotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_pivotal","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L111-L114","doc":"`Tr K = (1 + q²)²`: the two-site normaliser. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.qtrace_rHecke_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.qtrace_rHecke_div","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L105-L109","doc":"Hence the quantum trace of one generator, normalised by `Tr K = (1+q²)²`,\nis the convention-D loop value `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:categorical-trace-is-the-markov-trace","label":"rem:categorical-trace-is-the-markov-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-trace-is-the-markov-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.qtrace_rHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.qtrace_rHecke","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**Fact 3.** `Tr(K Ř) = q³(1 + q²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rHecke_hecke_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rHecke_hecke_relation","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L90-L96","doc":"**Fact 2.** The Hecke relation `(Ř − q)(Ř + q⁻¹) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.swap4_mul_swap4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.swap4_mul_swap4","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L84-L88","doc":"The swap is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.diagPart_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.diagPart_one","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L79-L82","doc":"The diagonal part vanishes at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rHecke_eq_swap_add_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rHecke_eq_swap_add_diag","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L73-L77","doc":"**Fact 1.** `Ř = s + D(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pivotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pivotal","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L69-L71","doc":"The pivotal weight `K = diag(1, q², q², q⁴)` on the pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rHecke","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L62-L67","doc":"The R-matrix in Hecke normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.diagPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.diagPart","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L58-L60","doc":"The diagonal part `D(q) = diag(q−1, 0, q−q⁻¹, q−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.swap4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.swap4","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPictureGenerator.lean#L51-L56","doc":"The swap on `ℂ² ⊗ ℂ²` in the basis `(e₁₁, e₁₂, e₂₁, e₂₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}